From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 14:56:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Enterprise security hardening: deny-by-default API auth,
 billing-gated upgrades, durable stores
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- ApiAuthGuardMiddleware: every /api endpoint denies unauthenticated requests
  when Auth:Enabled (live-config, fail-closed); [AllowAnonymous] on health/
  models/capabilities/plans keeps probes and pricing public. Builder-time
  RequireAuthorization() kept as defense in depth.
- Plan upgrades now require X-Auricrux-Billing-Key matching Billing:UpgradeApiKey
  (constant-time compare); disabled entirely when unset — closes the
  honor-system self-upgrade hole.
- FCA account links persisted to SQLite (fca_links.db); star-rating feedback
  persisted to SQLite (feedback.db) — both survive restarts.
- CSP: drop unsafe-eval, add object-src/base-uri/form-action; Kestrel body cap
  16MB; Microsoft.Data.Sqlite 8.0.11 -> 10.0.10 and SQLitePCLRaw bundle 3.0.5
  (clears GHSA-2m69-gcr7-jv3q); vulnerable-package sweep clean.
- Tests: auth gating (5 new), billing key (3), durable stores (3).
